seg-b8d1d45df70b = <b>What the record measures matters.</b> A servo log (linuxptp, chrony) records the offset the daemon measured and is correcting: it is the time error left under servo control, not an independent measurement of the clock against UTC. During the holdover step of a test that really removes the reference, a servo log still shows what the daemon believed, which can differ from the true error. A TICC or other counter against an independent reference is the stronger record; say which one you used when you report the result.

