seg-38eb634b7f8f = What the report holds

# text
# c1: steps
seg-6a64755e11d6 = <b><c1/></b>: for the baseline, the holdover and the recovery, the start and end, the sample count and the mean, rms, largest and end values of the time error.

# text
# c1: masks
seg-cd11d0838c44 = <b><c1/></b>: each mask you named, measured on the step its condition names. A mask written for a locked clock is measured on the baseline; one written for holdover or an autonomous clock on the holdover. Each check has its limit, the measured value, the margin and the table it is transcribed from. A mask that needs a longer record than the step gave is <b>INCOMPLETE</b>, never extrapolated; one the engine cannot evaluate for the record's sample interval is <b>NOT-EVALUATED</b> with the reason.

# text
# c1: holdover
seg-cb54e67ca4eb = <b><c1/></b>: the fractional frequency offset the system held (the slope of a least-squares line through the holdover time error, in ns/s, which is parts per billion), the residual about that line, the largest absolute time error and when it occurred, and the step at the moment of removal.

# text
# c1: holdover_envelope
# c2: locked_duration_days
seg-daa40ac07396 = <b><c1/></b>: the ePRTC-A holdover envelope of ITU-T G.8272.1 Table { "3" }, from <c2/>, with the time at which it is first exceeded.

# text
# c1: budgets
seg-cd480a1bf901 = <b><c1/></b>: the time after removal at which each time-error budget is first exceeded.

# text
# c1: recovery
# c2: |TE|
seg-007a0393cb39 = <b><c1/></b>: whether <c2/> came inside the band and stayed for the dwell time, how long after GNSS returned that started, the peak after restoration and the largest step between consecutive samples while recovering.

# text
# c1: curves
seg-199497dfcc09 = <b><c1/></b>: MTIE and TDEV of the baseline and holdover steps.

# text
